{"name":"Blackwood","hex":"#494e52","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Blackwood","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Any of many places around the world.\nA number of places in the United Kingdom:\nA hamlet north-east of Loch Carron, Highland council area, Scotland .\nAn outer suburb west of Cumbernauld, North Lanarkshire council area, Scotland .\nA village in South Lanarkshire council area, Scotland .\nA town and community in Caerphilly borough, Wales . \nA number of places in the United States:\nAn unincorporated community in Gordon County, Georgia.\nA census-designated place in Gloucester Township, Camden County, New Jersey. \nAn unincorporated community in Orange County, North Carolina.\nAn unincorporated community and coal town in Wise County, Virginia.\nA suburb of Adelaide, in the City of Mitcham, South Australia.\nA village in the Shire of Moorabool, north-west of Melbourne, Victoria, Australia.","A number of places in the United Kingdom:\nA hamlet north-east of Loch Carron, Highland council area, Scotland .\nAn outer suburb west of Cumbernauld, North Lanarkshire council area, Scotland .\nA village in South Lanarkshire council area, Scotland .\nA town and community in Caerphilly borough, Wales ."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A bidding convention in contract bridge, used to explore the partnership's possession of aces, kings and in some variants the queen of trumps, to judge more precisely whether slam is likely to be a good contract."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Blackwood"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dalbergia melanoxylon","blocks":[{"text":"Dalbergia melanoxylon is a flowering plant in the subfamily Faboideae of the family Fabaceae, native to seasonally dry regions of Africa from Senegal east to Eritrea, to southern regions of Tanzania to Mozambique and south to the north-eastern parts of South Africa. The tree is an important timber species in its native areas; it is used in the manufacture of musical instruments, sculptures vinyago in Swahili language and fine furniture. Populations and genomic resources for genetic biodiversity maintenance in parts of its native range are threatened by overharvesting due to poor or absent conservation planning and by the species' low germination rates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Dalbergia_melanoxylon.jpg/330px-Dalbergia_melanoxylon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dalbergia_melanoxylon","wikidata":"Q83170"},{"title":"Erythrophleum africanum","blocks":[{"text":"Erythrophleum africanum, the African blackwood, is a legume species in the genus Erythrophleum found in savannahs of tropical Africa. It produces a gum similar to gum arabic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Erythrophleum_africanum_256739007.jpg/330px-Erythrophleum_africanum_256739007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erythrophleum_africanum","wikidata":"Q5396494"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Dalbergia_melanoxylon-CME-2016.jpg/500px-Dalbergia_melanoxylon-CME-2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Dalbergia_melanoxylon-CME-2016.jpg/1280px-Dalbergia_melanoxylon-CME-2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Dalbergia_melanoxylon-CME-2016.jpg/500px-Dalbergia_melanoxylon-CME-2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"African blackwood in a garden in Pune, India, showing its rounded, irregular canopy with low branching and coppicing.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADalbergia_melanoxylon-CME-2016.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wiki